  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 24d0b860ee; owner-requested re-check of the 51 open P2 violated/todo_hard/todo_soft items; fixtures and outputs under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p2_review_11012026/C1/). VERDICT: CURRENT, and the item's 'second reading' (a product bug, not an environment dependency) is confirmed. On tmpfs (readdir = reverse creation order): JS files created a_early then z_late -> rglob [main, z_late, a_early] -> dst a_early PASS; created z_late then a_early -> rglob [main, a_early, z_late] -> dst z_late/utils.js:1-1:process:function FAIL. LLVM: created utils then main PASS; main then utils -> dst llvm_ir:main.ll:1-1:utility_func:declaration FAIL. `scripts/smart-test --no-cov <both node ids>` -> 2 passed (pytest tmp_path creates in the passing order here). Code: js_ts.py:7442/7771 global_symbols[sym.name] = sym (last-writer-wins); find_js_ts_files (:286) does not sort; the namespace path_hint lookup (:7191) does not override the name-keyed table; in LLVM a `declare` overwrites the `define` of the same name. The test docstring's 'rglob processes alphabetically' is false. PROPOSED (owner): split - (a) js namespace path_hint does not disambiguate same-name functions; (b) llvm declare shadows define; (c) make both tests create files in the failing order, or sort discovery. ROOT-CAUSE GROUP: symbol identity keyed by bare name in enumeration order (with INV-dosoz, INV-tohuj). Status unchanged."  # dc05
